    {
      "id": "dev-notes-3-comment-5036450568",
      "type": "comment",
      "repository": "web2026-dev-notes",
      "issueNumber": 3,
      "issueTitle": "Day 2: HTML, CSS and Commitment",
      "day": 2,
      "commentId": 5036450568,
      "content": "### **Day 2- Ugly web & CSS dinner**\nHad a great fun today, creating an ugly web made me try a lot of different things in CSS. The concept of making it ugly really made my mind free to explore CSS. \nAlso, the game was too informative and practical, which made me jump directly into the playground in a creative way without getting bored.\nOn the other hand traditional method (learning step by step, like syntax/property-wise)could have been like deep learning , but would have waisted lot of time. and that dosent make sense. \nInshort it was good learning day today. \njust wished that we could have a lil more time just playing around this ugly web, although it is not necessary. \n\n### INSHORT a big thumbs up for the day \n```\n      _\n     /(|\n    (  :\n   __\\  \\  _____\n (____)  `|\n(____)|   |\n (____).__|\n  (___)__.|_____\n```\n             ",
      "urls": [],
      "wordCount": 147,
